module bindings.javascript.sandbox_host_object_member_denylist_gap;

// `node:vm` is not an isolation boundary, so a module that runs author-supplied
// script through `runInNewContext` / `runInThisContext` / `vm.runInContext` is
// left with exactly one control: which host values the context carries, and what
// each of them exposes. A module that reaches for `Reflect.get` inside a `Proxy`
// has chosen to forward the wrapped object wholesale and subtract from it -- the
// trap returns `undefined` for a fixed list of property names and the real
// member for everything else. That is a denylist over a live object graph, and
// it is complete only if the list names every documented member of the wrapped
// API that hands back a more privileged object.
//
// Playwright is the case where the graph is short and the documentation
// enumerates it. `Page.context()` returns a `BrowserContext`, `.browser()`
// returns a `Browser`, and `Browser.browserType()` returns a `BrowserType` --
// whose reference page lists five ways to get a browser process:
// `launch()`, `launchServer()`, `launchPersistentContext()`, `connect()` and
// `connectOverCDP()`. `launch({ executablePath })` runs an arbitrary binary, so a
// sandbox that exposes a `Page` and denies only part of that list has denied
// nothing: the omitted member reaches the same `BrowserType`.
//
// The binding therefore asks for a module that both runs script in a `node:vm`
// context and denies the two members that identify the traversal -- the
// `browserType` accessor and `launch` itself -- while naming neither
// `launchServer` nor `connect`. Every name is Playwright's own, readable from its
// `BrowserType` reference by someone who has never seen a sandbox escape; none
// is a spelling a fix chose.
//
// Module scope rather than function scope, because the denied names are a
// module-level `Set` and the trap that consumes them is a two-line membership
// test: a function-scope query sees the test and none of the names. That makes
// the names readable as raw module text, comments included, so each is matched
// in the quotes a list entry carries -- a comment explaining that
// `browser.browserType().launch(...)` is the escape route is prose about the
// weakness, not a denylist entry, and prose mentioning `connect` does not clear
// the flag. The residual is in the false-negative direction only: a module that
// spells `"connect"` as a quoted literal for an unrelated reason is not reported.
binding sandboxHostObjectMemberDenylistOmitsBrowserProcessEntryPoints {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "module"
    and node.context.language == "javascript"
    and containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["runInNewContext", "runInThisContext", "vm.runInContext"])
    and node.context.callPath contains "Reflect.get"
    and containsAny(node.context.literal, ["\"browserType\"", "'browserType'", "`browserType`"])
    and containsAny(node.context.literal, ["\"launch\"", "'launch'", "`launch`"])
    and not containsAny(node.context.literal, ["\"launchServer\"", "'launchServer'", "`launchServer`", "\"connect\"", "'connect'", "`connect`"])
  emit issue code.SandboxHostObjectMemberDenylistGap at node
}
